From e276e41008a4b81a71e82fd130206ab4803e6173 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: johnnykang101 <johnny.kang101@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Mar 2026 20:36:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 047/127] ci: add concurrency group to beta workflow to prevent
 queue pile-up

Without a concurrency group the hourly cron kept adding new runs while
old ones were stuck queued, accumulating 24+ stale runs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .github/workflows/beta.yml | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/beta.yml b/.github/workflows/beta.yml
index a7106667b..f96867b03 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/beta.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/beta.yml
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@ on:
   schedule:
     - cron: "0 * * * *"
 
+concurrency:
+  group: beta-sync
+  cancel-in-progress: true
+
 jobs:
   sync:
     runs-on: blacksmith-4vcpu-ubuntu-2404
-- 
2.43.0

